<p>Was asked to take a look at this via PM.</p>
<p>I'm moderately concerned by your reliance in Series I articles to carry some key details of the article. Crosslinking is alright, but crosslinking to S1 in this way is a tad strange.</p>
<p>Additionally, I've got some issues with the idea of the people in the mirrors — it comes off as comical more than anything? Like, my reflection insulting me and demanding to be free doesn't spark feelings of fear or dread, just mild bemusement.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Therefore, researchers speculate that SCP-XXXX unique condition isn't to cause the desynchronisity, but to maintain synchronicity.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This is like though. The idea that she doesn't act as the impetus, but is instead the stopgap, makes for a good end-of-article twist. I'm also getting strong themes of self-dissatisfaction/hatred when looking at your reflection, something I'm down with examining. The basic anomalous properties just seems rather, uh, ill-fitting for the atmosphere I'm picking up.</p>

