<p>How about this for a flow of the story:</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Idea&nbsp;here</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Long,&nbsp;I&nbsp;know</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<ol>
<li>We start off with SCP-XXXX's discovery in 1945 when Farringford House is sold. As well as SCP-XXXX, they also discover a number of old documents which show sketches of SCP-XXXX's mutilations and a log of her time in the home. At the same time, the first recorded incident of SCP-XXXX-1 occurs.</li>
</ol>
<ol>
<li>The second incident of SCP-XXXX-1 occurs. Thanks to some decryption of the documents found with SCP-XXXX, the foundation makes the connection between SCP-XXXX and SCP-XXXX-1 and containment procedures are created accordingly.</li>
</ol>
<ol>
<li>An attempt to get some answers from SCP-XXXX are logged in an interview. She claims she doesn't remember her life before the house and only remembers weaving and her condition came because of a man. She is upset and gives vague answers to the questions before remaining silent. As the interview ends, she asks about the condition of 'Edward'. When they ask who 'Edward' is, SCP-XXXX quiets up again, only saying 'the shadows<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-842802-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-842802-1')">1</a></sup> made him sick. Sick on the inside'.</li>
</ol>
<ol>
<li>Further documentation about SCP-XXXX is found in Chapel House<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-842802-2" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-842802-2')">2</a></sup>. Also found is a logbook which details some of the past SCP-XXXX incidents, the 'decaying' process as well as Edwards descent into mental instability. One entire highlights the success of their endeavours to make SCP-XXXX ageless and give her her eyelid coatings. The logbook also mentions some members of the Pre-Raphaelite Brotherhood and their involvement with SCP-XXXX.</li>
</ol>
<ol>
<li>The third incident of SCP-XXXX-1 occurs. Following this two, a number of interviews are done with some of the victims. Most are sickened by the event and demonstrate an irrational fear of reflective surfaces. In the interviews, the victims claim their reflections spoke to them, with some screaming with rage, others degrading with vile slander and some just outright maliciously laughing or taunting<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-842802-3" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-842802-3')">3</a></sup>.</li>
</ol>
<ol>
<li>As a result of SCP-XXXX-1, a number of its victims have developed mental illnesses, depression, severe paranoia or psychosis, even after administering amnestics<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-842802-4" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-842802-4')">4</a></sup>. Some have descended into a state of such delirium, they have resorted to making irrational decisions such as removing fingernails, avoiding water or destroying computers and smart devices. A small amount has committed suicide too.</li>
</ol>
<ol>
<li>Final interview with SCP-XXXX. After being unresponsive for a few minutes, she begins talking about the shadows. When pressed about why she must remain alive, as her condition seems to cause SCP-XXXX-1, SCP-XXXX provides an answer which enables the foundation to understand that she is in fact preventing SCP-XXXX-1.</li>
</ol>
<ol>
<li>Final entry. After a health check-up, researcher's discover that SCP-XXXX's eyelid coating is starting to noticeably decay. Research into recreating the material has begun and adjustments to SCP-XXXX's containment procedure is begin reevaluated. However, the likelihood of SCP-XXXX-1 occurring more frequently is highly possible.</li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
