			<div class="content" id="post-content-4823815">
									

<p>Not a greenlighted but you asked me to review so I shall deliver.</p>
<p>Firstly, I think that the idea of linking the SCP to the poem doesn't feel like it adds much to the story. There isn't much evidence stated saying that this is a definite fact, and it just feels like a thrown in unnecessary detail. You could likely improve this by directly linking the SCP to the author of the play in an addendum log. If you would like to be more subtle about it you could just elaborate on this more on the interview aspect.</p>
<p>Secondly, there doesn't seem to be much information on how the foundation got ahold of or found out about SCP-XXXX. Where was it found, when was it found, and how was it found? Again adding addendum logs can allow you to add this kind of information quite easily.</p>
<p>Lastly, maybe elaborate more on the earlier captors of SCP-XXXX, and maybe add something about how the methods the other foundation used worked. It doesn't have to be something like that, but just elaborating in general would make it better. I know this seems repetitive, but an addendum log would help with this as well if your main worry is that it cant fit into the story well.</p>
<p>I guess what I'm trying to say is that you should elaborate on some of the plotlines, or details or just remove them entirely. You can use addendum logs and interviews to get across these points relatively easily, and I think that this story just needs a bit of freshening up. Other than that it is a great SCP idea, and can become something good if you fill in these holes.</p>

