														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4837798">
									

<p>This feels somewhat reminiscent of <a href="/scp-4205">SCP-4205</a> in the way that the people affected by the anomaly react and like, what happens to them; and I'm not exactly sure how this ties into Elaine of Astolat.</p>
<p>Really my biggest concern with this, narratively speaking, is it feels very passive: there's not really any kind of narrative stakes or anything pulling the story forward; so it ends up feeling very flat. It feels like there really needs to be more of an indication of how the increase in -1 occurrences is causing the Foundation to more and more desperately look into this.</p>
<p>It also feels very flat: there's not a lot of growth or change between the start of the story and the end, and the only real difference I can see is that everyone knows more about what is going. It really feels like it needs something permanent to happen here: for the SCP to understand what is happening and change as a result, or for the Foundation to find stuff out and react by changing containment procedures or doing new experiments or something.</p>

							</div>

								
					
